  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the Frankenstein's monster wax figure via the text overlay",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the Frankenstein's monster wax figure, as the text 'feel that? it used to belong to bruce jenner!' implies a direct connection between the user's perception and the figure. The phrase 'feel that?' is a deictic that invites the user to experience or identify with the sensation or horror associated with the figure, thereby projecting the user's own perspective onto the visual entity. The user is not explicitly addressed with 'you' or 'me', but the rhetorical question 'feel that?' creates an implicit projection of the user's embodied experience onto the figure, making the user the implied subject of the sensation being described.",
